     "q": "Our facility is single-use. Do we still need WFI and pure steam?",
     "a": "Usually. In-house media and buffers need WFI, autoclaves need pure steam, and most plants keep stainless buffer tanks that need CIP and SIP. Demand is lower but peakier."
    },
    {
     "q": "Can a cell therapy facility run on PW?",
     "a": "For washers and autoclave feed, often yes. The EMA guideline sets WFI for every step of a cell-based product not sterilized afterwards, made on site or bought in."
    },
    {
     "q": "Is membrane WFI acceptable for biologics?",
     "a": "USP and Ph. Eur. 0169 both allow it. For EU markets, notify the GMP authority before use; some corporate standards still require distillation. Confirm product by product."
    },
    {
     "q": "Will clinical qualification carry into commercial production?",
     "a": "Most of it, if the design allowed for growth. New generation and outlets go through change control: usually IQ and OQ of the new section, then increased sampling."
